## 6. ExpertCache: Per-Layer Admission Slot Range Validation

**Component:** `include/strata/core/expert_cache.hpp` — `layer_slot_range()` and `admit()`

**Responsibilities:** Maps `(layer, expert)` pairs to VRAM slot indices. Per-layer admission restricts each layer to a contiguous slot range to prevent one layer from consuming all slots.

**Problem:** `layer_slot_range` computes `q = slots_ / n_layers_` and assigns `[l*q, (l+1)*q)` with the last layer taking the remainder. When `slots_ < n_layers_`, `q = 0` and every layer gets an empty range, so `admit` always returns `kNotResident` silently. The caller has no way to distinguish "cache too small for per-layer mode" from "cache is full."

**Proposed change:** Add a `per_layer_feasible()` predicate and log a warning at `open` time when per-layer admission is enabled but `slots_ < n_layers_`.

```diff
--- a/include/strata/core/expert_cache.hpp
+++ b/include/strata/core/expert_cache.hpp
@@ -95,6 +95,10 @@ public:
     void set_per_layer_admission(bool on) { per_layer_ = on; }
     bool per_layer_admission() const { return per_layer_; }
+    /// Whether per-layer admission can give every layer at least one slot.
+    bool per_layer_feasible() const { return slots_ >= n_layers_; }
     /// The slot range layer `l` may admit into under per-layer admission.  Exposed so a test can check it.
     void layer_slot_range(int64_t layer, int64_t& lo, int64_t& hi) const;
```

